Hi,

I liked Deducer a lot. I've been using it for various statistical
approaches in my experiments. I've an experiment which has split split
plot design.  Can I use Deducer for split split plot ANOVA?

Thanks

From u267c7c6c510dc8a2 at groups.google.com  Wed Apr 27 15:12:48 2011
From: u267c7c6c510dc8a2 at groups.google.com (Ian Fellows)
Date: Wed, 27 Apr 2011 15:12:48 +0000
Subject: Re: Split split plot ANOVA
Message-ID: <Z0LMkU71xDk.gsXELhSRVigJ@deducer.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <Z0LMkU71xDk.C49pkN3VrZAJ@deducer.groups.google.com>
References: <Z0LMkU71xDk.C49pkN3VrZAJ@deducer.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/deducer/c/Z0LMkU71xDk/m/gsXELhSRVigJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

No. In general an unbalanced split-split plot design requires linear mixed models (lme) and the balanced case can be done with aov. Niether of these are built into the GUI (you can of course use the command line though).

Best,
ian

